❗️ Last night, the Armed Forces of the Russian Federation carried out a massed strike by high-precision air- and ground-launched weapons as well as strike unmanned aerial vehicles, against defence industry enterprises and logistics centres in Kiev and the Kiev region, and against infrastructure facilities at the Yuzhny Port in Odessa Region used for the delivery and storage of military cargo, petroleum, oil, and lubricants intended to support the Armed Forces of Ukraine.

💥 The following targets were struck in Kiev:

▫️the Kiev radio-electronics enterprise (Radioniks LLC), which manufactures control systems for the FP-5 Flamingo cruise missile, FP-7 and FP-9 operational-tactical missiles, Neptune-MD guided missiles, and an analogue of the surface-to-air guided missiles of the S-300 air defence missile system (Project Klon). The enterprise is also engaged in the modernisation, technical maintenance and repair of onboard electro-optical targeting systems and airborne radars for MiG-29 aircraft;

▫️the Kiev rocket and space industry enterprise (Spetsoboronmash LLC / Artem State Joint-Stock Holding Company). It produces components of control systems for the FP-5 Flamingo cruise missile, FP-7 and FP-9 operational-tactical missiles, Neptune-MD guided missiles, and an analogue of the surface-to-air guided missiles of the S-300 air defence missile system (Project Klon);

▫️ the Kiev-90 manufacturing enterprise (Meridian named after Korolev LLC), which produces structural elements and components for guidance systems and various assemblies of Neptune-MD guided missiles;

▫️the Oaklayn LLC, Kiev. It manufactures components for long-range unmanned aerial vehicles of the Deep Strike type, produces carbon-fibre parts and batteries for FPV drones of various modifications, and also stores UAVs;

▫️ the Kiev sorting centre (Kiev Innovation Terminal of Novaya Pochta), which is used for the delivery and storage of dual-use products including those intended for the production of UAVs, robotic systems, and electronic warfare equipment.

The following targets were reportedly struck in Kiev Region:

▫️the Tarasovka logistics centre (Antel Properties), which receives, stores, assembles, and distributes individual components and assemblies for the production of long-range unmanned aerial vehicles.

💥 POL tanks intended to support the Armed Forces of Ukraine at the Yuzhny Port in Odessa Region were also engaged.

🔹 Russian Defence Ministry
